  vaem:acronym "AGPLv3.0" ;
  vaem:description "This is a free software, copyleft license. Its terms effectively consist of the terms of GPLv3, with an additional paragraph in section 13 to allow users who interact with the licensed software over a network to receive the source for that program. GNU AGPL v3.0 should be considered by Developers considering using the GNU AGPL for any software which will commonly be run over a network. Note that the GNU AGPL is not compatible with GPLv2. It is also technically not compatible with GPLv3 in a strict sense: you cannot take code released under the GNU AGPL and convey or modify it however you like under the terms of GPLv3, or vice versa. However, you are allowed to combine separate modules or source files released under both of those licenses in a single project, which will provide many programmers with all the permission they need to make the programs they want. " ;
  voag:incompatibleWith voag:GNU-GPL_V2 ;
  voag:supercedes voag:AGPL_V1PT0 ;
  voag:url "http://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl.html" .

